Independent readback
All10 negative-case64MiB targets were hashed in their entirety and matched
all pre-write bytes. All14 finite positive targets were compared by complete
expected-byte SHA256, including payload, unchanged middle and cleared tail.
The sparse >2TiB case checked the written first sector, final33 sectors and
seeded incorrect-low-address guard separately. The utility itself reread every
written payload and cleared-tail byte before displaying success.

Reproducibility
The Zero firmware composer regenerates both canonical source files byte for
byte from the shared Zero parts. All40 IA32 composition replacements must
match, including exact-once source insertion. Existing output paths are
refused. The composer retains a partial new output on failure, avoiding a
path-based cleanup race. IA32 page allocations are explicitly bounded below
4GiB using AllocateMaxAddress.

External test control used QEMU, OVMF and private host harnesses outside the
product tree. No physical USB hardware, native VirtualBox, BIOS writer or
in-kernel Zero USB driver is claimed. The application is a UEFI utility and
runs before ExitBootServices. Its source-volume filesystem and USB controller
support are provided by the firmware platform interface.
